commit 61de4aa23bbc27d49c51204e600119201ddd4b04
Author:     Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Sat Aug 22 00:11:05 2026 -0400
Commit:     Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sat Aug 22 00:11:05 2026 -0400

    exp_21: fa_cartesian is a first-class cond_method in eval_FLAC.py
    
    Round 3, part A (plan SS3d). The arm was trainable after round 2 but not
    measurable: eval_FLAC rejected 'fa_cartesian' in argparse and in the
    programmatic fail-fast, and orbit_provenance returned the NO-ORBIT pair for it.
    
    Every edit is an added branch or a widened membership test; vanilla and
    fa_invariant are untouched, pinned by the golden record/meta capture (key order
    included) in test_fa_cartesian_eval.py and by test_eval_paths.py staying
    byte-unchanged.
    
    Two module constants replace the per-site equality tests --
    FRAME_AVERAGED_COND_METHODS = ("fa_invariant", "fa_cartesian") and
    COND_METHODS = ("vanilla",) + those. Four sites have to agree about which
    methods are frame-averaged (provenance, the recorded angle list, the dispatch,
    argparse); a site that silently disagrees does not crash, it writes a plausible
    record. A row whose cond_method names an orbit method while frame_avg_angles and
    frame_avg_fwd_cap are null is exactly what the SS3g admission validator rejects
    -- and it would be rejected only after the GPU hours that produced it.
    
    Widened (before -> after):
     * orbit_provenance L810: == "fa_invariant" -> in FRAME_AVERAGED_COND_METHODS,
       so a fa_cartesian row records ("batched", <real cap>) instead of ("n/a", None).
     * evaluate_model fail-fast L1101: the literal tuple -> COND_METHODS, message
       enumerated from the constant.
     * frame_angles_record L1387: == "fa_invariant" -> membership, so the REAL angle
       list is recorded instead of null.
     * argparse --cond-method choices -> list(COND_METHODS).
    
    Added: the fa_cartesian_conditioning import and one dispatch branch in the eval
    loop, issuing the SAME call shape as the fa_invariant branch (four positional
    arguments plus max_fwd_samples= as a keyword) -- the arms differ in the function,
    not in how it is invoked.
    
    Deliberately NOT forked: the filename rule. build_output_paths already inserts
    _<cond_method>_a<n_angles> for every non-vanilla method, so _fa_cartesian_a4
    falls out of the existing rule unmodified (verified, then pinned by three tests).
    
    Frame-angle and cap resolution were already cond_method-agnostic and are shared
    as-is: the cap validator still fires before any file or model work, naming
    --frame-avg-max-fwd-samples. At --batch-size 64 the cap must be >= 64 (a chunk is
    whole angles), which the SS5 templates pass explicitly and the help text now
    states.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G8aU3GgbrkgdKK2PxWhZBV

