    exp_21: pin the eval-loop conditioning dispatch itself (coverage)
    
    Self-caught coverage defect of the same class the r2 review found on the
    training side. Every evaluate_model test in this file drives an EMPTY
    dataloader, so none of them executes the loop BODY: deleting the fa_cartesian
    dispatch branch left all 22 green while the arm silently evaluated as vanilla --
    a single-pass conditioning reported under a record claiming a C4 orbit, which is
    announcement 05's failure in its worst form (plausible numbers, wrong arm).
    
    Three tests now drive one real batch through the loop with only the sampler
    stubbed, asserting which function the dispatch called and that the raw
    single-pass conditioner was not used. The fa_invariant and vanilla cases are
    pinned the same way as regressions -- a new branch must not steal an existing
    one. The call SHAPE is pinned with them: conditioner/metadata/device plus the
    angle tuple positionally, max_fwd_samples as a keyword, identical to the
    fa_invariant branch.
    
    Mutation evidence for the round, each run against the full file:
      orbit_provenance narrowed to ==fa_invariant   -> 6 failed
      frame_angles_record narrowed                  -> 3 failed
