   461	    Distinct sources sit metres apart, so a fixed 6-decimal rendering identifies
   462	    the draw exactly while being byte-stable across machines.
   463	
   464	    Read BEFORE any rotation: ``rotate_scene_metadata`` rewrites ``context_poses``,
   465	    and a fingerprint taken afterwards would encode the rotation instead of the
   466	    item (and could never match its unrotated pair).
   467	
   468	    The rendering is FAIL-CLOSED on its own assumptions (review N4). A six-decimal
